I
# STRIPPED COPY - rows 1310/1311/1312/1313/1314 removed.
#
# This is what option 1 of spec section 7.3 looks like: Gateway serving an
# old client an apt.dat with the new rows taken out. 1301 alone is complete
# and authoritative by design (R1/R2), so nothing is lost except the
# refinements the old client could not have used anyway.
#
# Any WED can open this one. The unstripped original cannot be opened by any
# WED that does not know rows 1310-1313 - including, today, ours.
#
1200 Generated by hand for the WED livery format proposal - see README.md

1    3280 0 0 ZZLI Livery Format Sample
1302 city Livery Format Sample
1302 country USA
1302 datum_lat 38.900000000
1302 datum_lon -101.012000000
1302 gui_label 2D
1302 icao_code ZZLI
1302 region_code K1
100 45.00 26 0 0.25 0 2 1 09  38.90600000 -101.01200000 0 0 2 0 0 0 27  38.90600000 -100.98800000 0 0 2 0 0 0

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# POLICY DEFINITIONS. Scoped to this airport block, valid ANYWHERE in it (R6).
# Names are content-derived, generated by the writer - never author-supplied.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------


# 01-CONTROL
#   no new rows at all - the control. MUST be byte-identical to today.
1300  38.90000000 -101.01200000 000.0 gate jets 01-CONTROL
1301 C airline dal ual

# 02-PIN-C
#   pinned to class C. Always an A320/B738/MD82 from DAL or UAL.
1300  38.90000000 -101.01090343 000.0 gate jets 02-PIN-C
1301 C airline dal ual

# 03-MIX-CDE
#   C 60% / D 30% / E 10%. The distribution the old step-down could not
#   express.
1300  38.90000000 -101.00980687 000.0 gate heavy|jets 03-MIX-CDE
1301 E airline dal ual

# 04-ALL-ZERO
#   all-zero is LEGAL and means nothing spawns. Not an error.
1300  38.90000000 -101.00871030 000.0 gate jets 04-ALL-ZERO
1301 C airline dal ual

# 05-CLASS-F
#   weights point at F. The library ships NO F-class livery at all, so this is
#   permanently empty. Data gap, not a format error.
1300  38.90000000 -101.00761373 000.0 gate heavy 05-CLASS-F
1301 F airline dal ual baw

# 06-UNFILLABLE
#   THE 17.2% CASE. BAW has liveries at C and E but none at D, so this stand
#   is always empty. WED will REFUSE to export this (hard error + one-click
#   fix). Present here so the sim side can see what it looks like at runtime.
1300  38.90000000 -101.00651717 000.0 gate heavy|jets 06-UNFILLABLE
1301 D airline baw

# 07-POLICY-A
#   references a shared policy defined at the top of the block.
1300  38.90000000 -101.00542060 000.0 gate heavy|jets 07-POLICY-A
1301 E airline ual dal baw aal afr

# 08-POLICY-B
#   same policy as 07. This sharing is the 83%-of-stands case.
1300  38.90000000 -101.00432403 000.0 gate heavy|jets 08-POLICY-B
1301 E airline ual dal baw aal afr

# 09-FORWARD-REF
#   R6: the policy is defined AFTER this stand, at the end of the block. MUST
#   resolve.
1300  38.90000000 -101.00322747 000.0 gate jets 09-FORWARD-REF
1301 C airline dal ual

# 10-EXCLUDE
#   DAL at class C minus the 737 -> only A320 and MD82 may spawn.
1300  38.90000000 -101.00213090 000.0 gate jets 10-EXCLUDE
1301 C airline dal

# 11-BAD-5-WEIGHTS
#   V8: five weights. Drop the row WHOLE -> behaves like 01. MUST NOT be read
#   as 0 0 10 0 0 0.
1300  38.90000000 -101.00103433 000.0 gate jets 11-BAD-5-WEIGHTS
1301 C airline dal ual

# 12-BAD-DECIMAL
#   V12: a decimal point is never legal here. Drop whole -> behaves like 01.
1300  38.90000000 -100.99993776 000.0 gate jets 12-BAD-DECIMAL
1301 C airline dal ual

# 13-BAD-NEGATIVE
#   V10: negative weight. Drop whole -> behaves like 01.
1300  38.90000000 -100.99884120 000.0 gate jets 13-BAD-NEGATIVE
1301 C airline dal ual

# 14-DANGLING-REF
#   V13: reference to a policy that does not exist. Drop it -> behaves like
#   01.
1300  38.90000000 -100.99774463 000.0 gate jets 14-DANGLING-REF
1301 C airline dal ual

# 15-MIXED-EXCL
#   V15: one bad exclusion among two good ones. Drop ONLY 'garbage'; both real
#   exclusions still apply.
1300  38.90000000 -100.99664806 000.0 gate jets 15-MIXED-EXCL
1301 C airline dal ual

# 16-UNKNOWN-ROW
#   V18/R15: an unknown row code must be ignored, not rejected.
1300  38.90000000 -100.99555150 000.0 gate jets 16-UNKNOWN-ROW
1301 C airline dal ual

# 17-1301-WINS
#   V17: the policy lists dal AND ual, but 1301 lists only dal. 1301 is
#   authoritative (R3) - ual must never spawn here.
1300  38.90000000 -100.99445493 000.0 gate jets 17-1301-WINS
1301 C airline dal

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Defined AFTER the stand that uses it, on purpose. R6 says this must resolve:
# a 'definitions must precede use' rule is broken by moving two lines, and the
# reader already buffers one airport at a time.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

99
